        "biography": "Anita Overland began her career producing commercials and music videos for director Gerard de Thame before transitioning into line-producing films. She produced her first short film,\u00a0Syrup, which won the Cannes Film Festival Jury Prize and received an Oscar nomination. Her credits include\u00a0The Tribe\u00a0for Stephen Poliakoff, the TV series\u00a0The Book Group\u00a0directed by Annie Griffin, and\u00a0In This World\u00a0for Andrew Eaton and Michael Winterbottom, which won the Special Achievement prize at the BIFAs and Best Film in a Foreign Language at the BAFTAs. Additionally, she worked as a co-producer on\u00a0A Mighty Heart,\u00a0A Cock and Bull Story, and\u00a0The Young Victoria. Overland also produced the\u00a0Red Riding trilogy for Revolution Films.",
